@	
s	am	Returns the invoker's real user name
o	-a	Same as -bdlprTtu	
o	-b	Time of last system boot	
o	-d	Print dead processes	
o	-H	Write column headings above the regular output	
o	-l	Print system login processes (unsupported)	
o	-m	Only print information about the current terminal	
o	-p	Print active processes spawned by launchd(8) (unsupported)	
o	-q	'Quick mode': List only names and number of users currently logged on	
o	-r	Print the current runlevel	
o	-s	List only the name, line and time fields (this is the default)	
o	-T	Print a character after the user name indicating the state of the terminal line: '+' writable, '-'…	
o	-t	Print last system clock change (unsupported)	
o	-u	Print the idle time for each user and the associated process ID	
a	1	0
